  "deskripsi": "Ticket board kept as markdown files in a repo's `.kerjaan/` folder, one subfolder per status (backlog, todo, in_progress, review, done, cancel). Use it to create, move, edit, cancel or list tickets, to start a board, and to work the queue through worker and reviewer agents. Trigger it on indirect asks too, like \"note this down for later\", \"put that on the backlog\", \"not now, maybe later\", \"mark that as done\", \"what are we working on\", \"work the queue\", or in Indonesian \"catat ini dulu\", \"tandai sudah selesai\", \"apa saja yang sedang dikerjakan\", \"kerjakan tiket berikutnya\". In a repo without `.kerjaan/`, words like review, done or todo alone mean ordinary code work, not this skill. Prefer it over an ad-hoc TODO list or notes file.",
